<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Petrobras finds oil off northeast coast.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Petrobras finds oil off northeast coast.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian state-owned oil monopoly Petrobras has announced the discovery of a new oilfield off the coast of the northeastern state of Sergipe.</p>
<p>The new oilfield 18 km off the coast is estimated to have oil and natural gas reserves of 5 million barrels per day (bpd), Petrobras said in a statement.</p>
<p>The reserves are located at a depth of 1,320 meters.</p>
<p>At present, the state of Sergipe produces 39,000 bpd of oil and 2 million cubic meters of natural gas a day.</p>
<p>-- Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151</p>
